# Pinned asn1c toolchain for regenerating this tree (issue #223).
#
# Single machine-readable source of truth for the generator version:
# .github/workflows/asn1c-regen.yml sources this file, rebuilds the exact
# toolchain below and re-runs the gen-s1ap/gen-ngap targets, failing the
# job when the regenerated output drifts from the committed tree.
#
# The pin is mouse07410/asn1c v1.5.3 (tag commit e6c2799a, 2026-10-07;
# issue #521). It carries the upstream fixes for GHSA-x882-jvjm-xxh9
# (ce45145ad4) and GHSA-rcj5-gcvg-x796 (e9600cf7f2), so the recipe applies
# no runtime patch (issue #522 dropped the #513 backports).
#
# Flag mapping: v1.5.x removed -gen-PER (split at b5ed2c1f into
# -gen-UPER/-gen-APER) and generates every codec by default. The recipe
# maps -gen-PER to -gen-APER — the dissectors decode aligned PER only —
# and passes -no-gen-UPER -no-gen-JER -no-gen-CBOR (src/mmt_mobile/asn1c/
# Makefile, ASN1C_CODECS). ASN1C_PREFIX (ngap/ naming) is unchanged.
#
# Version string: v1.5.x computes it at autoreconf time from
# `git describe` and the commit date, and falls back to NOGIT-<build date>
# in a tarball, which every generated file header embeds. The recipe
# therefore stamps ASN1C_VERSION_STRING and ASN1C_BUGURL into configure.ac
# before autoreconf: the string is what `git describe --tags --long` of the
# tag reports, the URL is upstream's tarball fallback. `asn1c -v` must
# print exactly "ASN.1 Compiler, ${ASN1C_VERSION_STRING} (${ASN1C_BUGURL})".
ASN1C_REPO=mouse07410/asn1c
ASN1C_REF=e6c2799ac9e64702dd425b47d838aa27b2495e7b
ASN1C_REF_NAME=v1.5.3
ASN1C_VERSION=1.5.3
ASN1C_VERSION_STRING=v1.5.3-0-ge6c2799a-2026-10-07
ASN1C_BUGURL=https://github.com/mouse07410/asn1c/issues
ASN1C_TARBALL_SHA256=51da7f833ba88a513844df66c5c7027f5a26ad5722a3a2c31db40116fb7aa229
